        "With the partial: true option (and Minimatch#match(path, true)), a path should match when it is a valid prefix of a path that the full pattern could match, including when the pattern contains **. Today patterns with a globstar wrongly report false for valid prefixes. For example minimatch(\"/b/c/d/a\", \"/**/a/b/c\", { partial: true }), minimatch(\"/b/c/d/a\", \"/**/a/b/c/**\", { partial: true }), minimatch(\"a\", \"a/**\", { partial: true }), minimatch(\"/b/c/d/a\", \"/**/a/**/b/c/**\", { partial: true }) and minimatch(\"/b/c/d/a\", \"/**/a/**\", { partial: true }) must all return true, while minimatch(\"b/a\", \"a/**\", { partial: true }) must still return false. Existing partial behavior for patterns without ** (for example \"/a/b\" against \"/*/b/x/y/z\" is true and \"/a/b/c\" is false) and makeRe(pattern, { partial: true }) must be unchanged, and non-partial matching must not loosen: minimatch(\"/b/c/d/a\", \"/**/a/b/c\") stays false. Make the change in the ** path-walking logic in src/index.ts, not by post-processing results. The library is TypeScript built with npx tshy; tests run with npm test (tap, which requires 100% coverage).\n\nVisible acceptance check (it must pass; it is not the only criterion): npx tshy && node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: npm test\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/.\n\nThe checks below still fail after the previous attempt in this workspace. Fix them in the\nsame workspace; the earlier edits are still present.\n\nvisible check (npx tshy && node acceptance/visible/check.mjs) exited 1:\nnode:internal/modules/run_main:107\n    triggerUncaughtException(\n    ^\n\nAssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: Expected values to be strictly equal:\n\nfalse !== true\n\n    at file:///Users/brad/.cache/swarm-comparison/work/visible-minimatch-bugfix-partial-globstar-ZcfI6G/checkout/acceptance/visible/check.mjs:3:8\n    at ModuleJob.run (node:internal/modules/esm/module_job:437:25)\n    at async no